{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/798547-alpha-predators-the-strongest-vampires","id":798547,"title":"Alpha Predators: The Strongest Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T18:56:32-08:00","id":798547,"title":"Alpha Predators: The Strongest Vampires","content":"Challenge: create a vampire at the heights of Kindred power. Start with the basic character creation. You gain 45 Experiences to raise Blood Potency to 10. You have 250 Experiences for everything else. You must create an actual character, not a one-dimensional white-room collection of numbers. Describe at least in brief how you might play this character, or her background, fill in some details. Go into as much detail as you like, but give us at least a little context. What can the character do? How have her supernatural strengths and frailties changes her life or distanced her from humanity? Does she embrace her role as an inhuman predator or does she try to stay grounded somehow? How has she managed to stay so strong without succumbing to torpor\u2014or does it loom just around the corner?<br /> <br /> Make an undead god of blood and hunger. Give it some (un)life and who knows? Maybe one day you'll get to play that character. We can always run through some scenarios once we have some characters and a sense of their place, see what it's like to stalk the night as a predator of vast and horrific power.<br /> <br /> For the record, here are Experience costs to raise Attributes and Skills (starting at 1 for Skills or the average for Attributes) to maximum:<br /> <br /> Attribute (2-10): 32<br /> Skill (1-10): 18<br /> <br /> I'll participate, too, once I nail down a concept. I like the Gangrel best, so perhaps a Gangrel of the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T19:13:00-08:00","id":798554,"title":"","content":"Is Unnatural affinity cheating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T21:15:21-08:00","id":798942,"title":"","content":"I'll report back with the spider at the web of some sort of hideous globe-spanning financial conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T22:02:55-08:00","id":799045,"title":"","content":"I wanna do a Gangrel Ordo member too... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Translation: I've got someone terrifying for you all to meet.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T22:40:26-08:00","id":799072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/798547-alpha-predators-the-strongest-vampires?p=798554#post798554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Unnatural affinity cheating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all! But it deserves a mention of how your vampire is making use of it. Feeding from werewolves is all well and fine in theory, but in practice it is tough unless you have something really unusual worked out. Which you might! This is a chance to flex your creative muscles by building a character at a level you'll rarely get to see in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T23:10:06-08:00","id":799076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/798547-alpha-predators-the-strongest-vampires?p=799072#post799072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all! But it deserves a mention of how your vampire is making use of it. Feeding from werewolves is all well and fine in theory, but in practice it is tough unless you have something really unusual worked out. Which you might! This is a chance to flex your creative muscles by building a character at a level you'll rarely get to see in play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My vague idea is the Mehket level 2 masquerade. A hoarder of secrets who's profound curiousity is what keeps him going. He's always a neonate of Ancilla in whatever Covanant is his current interest. When he feels he's learned enough or gotten too &quot;important&quot; he &quot;dies&quot; or &quot;falls into torpor&quot; judicious use of obfuscate and dominate and some new sire &quot;Remembers' embracing him just last night in a new city...<br /> <br /> Along the way he's joined packs and cults, followed along on the pilgrmage always trying to eek out just abit more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T23:45:38-08:00","id":799091,"title":"","content":"I love this! I'm writing my acolyte daeva right now. I really like building exceptionally strong characters like this, just at least to see what they can do and how massive I can get their dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T00:02:42-08:00","id":799114,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I love it too. Working on an Invictus Ventrue myself, gonna see how much of a tyrant I can make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10665-awkwardturtle","name":"AwkwardTurtle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10665_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T06:04:14-08:00","id":799562,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#373e4d\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Here is my Alpha Predator, Vaiur The Wild King. He is a Crone Nosferatu who excels in Cruac and other disciplines and has a chip on his shoulder, due his long dead Mother.<br /> Hope you guys like him !</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=16fZ_V1TGMnvwtG3bc2Jb1g22bHGTIWVmBAV21Pj8lVw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=16fZ_V1TGMnvwtG3bc2Jb1g22bHGTIWVmBAV21Pj8lVw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=16fZ_V1TGMnvwtG3bc2Jb1g22bHGTIWVmBAV21Pj8lVw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=16fZ_V1TGMnvwtG3bc2Jb1g22bHGTIWVmBAV21Pj8lVw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10405-lithiumdhalia","name":"LithiumDhalia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T08:33:26-08:00","id":799633,"title":"","content":"Are bloodlines open?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:08:05-08:00","id":799683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/798547-alpha-predators-the-strongest-vampires?p=799633#post799633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are bloodlines open?</div> </div> </div> </div>I too am curious, particularly because a lot of of my elder concepts include a bloodlines that are not 2e compliant yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:36:47-08:00","id":799696,"title":"","content":"Here is mine, an ancient Mekhet from Carthage traveling the world to figure out the <s>World</s> Chronicles of Darkness:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10D6hDaLn3O_CuxiMo8W2ob98GfdE633bWVY2CO8L21M/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> On the topic of Bloodlines, I ignored it for him. I could imagine some cool ideas for Gifts and Banes, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T10:45:28-08:00","id":799699,"title":"","content":"I don't see why Bloodlines wouldn't be allowed, especially since you're not putting the character into play and the suggestion that they might have 5 dots of a bloodline discipline would be enough to get across that they are masters of their bloodline's magic.<br /> <br /> I was torn between a khaibit and a Child of Judas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T12:22:30-08:00","id":799735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/798547-alpha-predators-the-strongest-vampires?p=799699#post799699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why Bloodlines wouldn't be allowed, especially since you're not putting the character into play and the suggestion that they might have 5 dots of a bloodline discipline would be enough to get across that they are masters of their bloodline's magic.<br /> <br /> I was torn between a khaibit and a Child of Judas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Children of Judas are my favorite bloodline. I'll probably do one of them or a Morbus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T13:03:08-08:00","id":799762,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines are totally acceptable. If they're not in 2E already, you may have to provide some quick notes on what they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:36:00-08:00","id":800389,"title":"","content":"I have some ideas for a Sanctified Gangrel of the Kerberos Bloodline, that I am working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T03:40:42-08:00","id":800486,"title":"","content":"Are there any deadlines to the task, Claire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quo